      "widgets_values": [
        "CORE-ONLY CONTROL — does stock ref2va put a reference image in frame 0?\n\nZero custom nodes. But that is NOT enough on its own: ComfyUI-H3-Toolkit\nreplaces PackedLayout process-wide the moment it imports, so this graph still\nruns on our row positioning unless the pack is DISABLED.\n\nTO RUN THE CONTROL PROPERLY:\n  1. disable custom_nodes/ComfyUI-H3-Toolkit\n  2. restart ComfyUI\n  3. confirm the log does NOT say 'PackedLayout patched'\n  4. point the three LoadImage nodes at the same character anchors\n  5. run\n\nREAD: if frame 0 is still the reference photo, this is core/model behaviour\nand nothing in our pack is implicated. If frame 0 is clean, our PackedLayout\nreplacement is placing reference rows on the target timeline and that is a\nreal bug in video.py.\n\nGeometry, seed and sampler match the H3 02 run being investigated: 576x1056,\n192 frames, ref_image_size 'match', seed 2024, res_multistep/simple/20/1.0,\nshift 12/3. The prompt is a plain-text equivalent of what H3ScenePrompt\ncompiled -- close, not identical, which is fine for this question."
